    "result_text": "The test passes. \n\nThe change is minimal and low structural impact: a single edit to `NormalizeOwnerEmail.service`, the class already responsible for email validation. It already rejects syntactically invalid emails with a 400 via `MissingOwnerFieldsException`, so a disposable-domain rejection follows the exact same pattern \u2014 no new files, no new exception/handler/escalation YAML, and no other function or class grown. `NormalizeOwnerEmail` has no other methods (WMC_other = 0), so the added branch stays cheap.\n\nImplementation:\n- Added a `DISPOSABLE_DOMAINS` set (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`).\n- After lower-casing, extract the domain (portion after `@`, already guaranteed present by the syntax check) and reject with 400 if it's blocklisted.\n\n`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0 \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.`",
